# Typed DTOs — TokenRealty

Human doc: [docs/rules/java-dtos.md](../../docs/rules/java-dtos.md).

## Required

- **Controllers:** `@RequestBody` and return types are **records or classes** — never `Map`, `Object`, or raw `List<?>`.
- **List endpoints:** return `Page<ResponseDto>` — never expose JPA entities.
- **Mutations:** return typed response records (`PaymentResponse`, `OrderResponse`) — not `Object`.
- **Validation:** `@Valid` on request records; Bean Validation on fields.

## Forbidden in API / service layers

```java
// BAD
public Object initiatePayment(...) { return Map.of("status", "PENDING"); }
public Page<Map<String, Object>> listPayments();
```

```java
// GOOD
public PaymentResponse initiate(@Valid @RequestBody InitiatePaymentRequest req);
public Page<PaymentResponse> listPayments(Pageable pageable);
```

## File layout

**Layered** (registry, issuance):

```
dto/PropertyDtos.java       # grouped request/response records
client/                     # downstream API response records
kafka/events/               # typed event payload records (target)
```

**Hexagonal** (marketplace, auth, payment):

```
dto/                        # OK today
adapter/in/web/dto/         # preferred when refactoring
kafka/events/               # ListingCreatedEvent, PaymentConfirmedEvent, …
```

Group related records in `*Dtos.java` holder classes — do not nest large types on controllers.

## Allowed exceptions

- **Validation errors:** `Map<String, String>` field errors inside `GlobalExceptionHandler` only.
- **External boundaries:** parse Hardhat/Web3j JSON as `Map` — convert to typed result immediately.
- **Outbox JSON column:** serialize typed event records; avoid building `Map<String, Object>` in publishers ([kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc)).

## Inter-service clients

Prefer typed records per downstream API. Map errors via [rest-client-errors.mdc](rest-client-errors.mdc).

```java
// GOOD — marketplace-service
public ComplianceCheckResponse checkWallet(String walletAddress);
```

## Mapping

- Controller: validate DTO → call service → map response.
- Entity → response: MapStruct mapper or static `from(entity)` on response record.
- Do not return JPA entities from controllers or assemble long field lists inline.

See [lombok.mdc](lombok.mdc), [spring-java-services.mdc](spring-java-services.mdc), [pagination.mdc](pagination.mdc).
